# Textual's /nick works once connected, before 001 (`isConnected`). A
# rejection of the typed nick is the server's answer to the user, printed
# to the console, and does not move the nick ladder; a rejection of the
# ladder's nick still does. 001 names the nick we got.
= nick taken
> CAP LS 302
> NICK taken
> USER textual 0 * Textual
< :irc.test 421 * CAP :Unknown command
! type console /nick mine
> NICK mine
< :irc.test 433 * mine :Nickname is already in use
? line console Message(433): mine Nickname is already in use
! type console nick other
> NICK other
< :irc.test 433 * taken :Nickname is already in use
> NICK taken_
? notice The nick taken is already in use; trying taken_
< :irc.test 001 other :Welcome other
? registered other
